# VVDN -- 6 synthetic departures in trail from real Gate 28, RWY 35R,
# real SID BUNTA 2G -- inter-departure timing derived from
# FTS Server/docs/VVDN-Trigger-Point-Consecutive-Departures.docx
# (Take-off Clearance Trigger Point analysis for VVDN RWY 35R).
# Callsigns VDN711-716 are SYNTHETIC. Fleet mix deliberately exercises
# all 4 real wake-turbulence-category pairings present at VVDN
# (MEDIUM/HEAVY only -- no SUPER/LIGHT in the real VVDN fleet):
#
#   VDN711 (MEDIUM) -> VDN712 (MEDIUM): gap = 60s -- PROVISIONAL -- ICAO 4444 Sec.5.6.1 blanket 1-min baseline; local 124-QD-CHK 1NM-diverging-heading reduction NOT applied here pending turn-initiation-altitude SOP data (see docx Sec.6)
#   VDN712 (MEDIUM) -> VDN713 (HEAVY): gap = 60s -- PROVISIONAL -- same basis as MEDIUM->MEDIUM above
#   VDN713 (HEAVY) -> VDN714 (MEDIUM): gap = 120s -- CONFIRMED -- ICAO Doc4444 5.8.3.1(3): 'LIGHT or MEDIUM aircraft taking off behind a HEAVY aircraft -- 2 minutes'
#   VDN714 (MEDIUM) -> VDN715 (HEAVY): gap = 60s -- PROVISIONAL -- same basis as MEDIUM->MEDIUM above
#   VDN715 (HEAVY) -> VDN716 (HEAVY): gap = 60s -- PROVISIONAL -- same basis as MEDIUM->MEDIUM above
#
# GROUND TRACK: taxi/roll/climb/SID profile is copied byte-for-byte
# from the proven, centerline-cross-checked VDN701 block in
# VVDN_GATE26_3DEP_RWY35R_BUNTA2G.scn (see that file's own header for
# full sourcing/limitations notes -- MOVE-based approximated physics,
# NOT per-type BADA performance; a live headless test this session
# confirmed that splicing real per-type BADA takeoff data onto a
# MOVE-taxied aircraft mid-scenario produces a broken ~0.1kt/s
# acceleration artifact, so the uniform MOVE-approximated profile is
# used for all 6 aircraft here, same as the proven template).
#
# GATE 28 (16.051747, 108.202278, gates.geojson, heading 80.9 deg) is
# real. The short PUSHBACK STUB bridging Gate 28 to the point where
# the route joins the real shared taxiway centerline is a LINEAR
# INTERPOLATION between the two real endpoints (disclosed
# approximation -- not independently re-derived from
# taxiway_centerlines.geojson for this exact short run, since Gate 28
# and Gate 26 are only ~140m apart and feed the same taxiway). Every
# point from the merge point onward is unchanged, real-centerline-
# verified data from the template.
#
# AIRCRAFT TYPES are real per-callsign (A320/A321/A20N -- MEDIUM;
# B788/B773/A332 -- HEAVY) for correct wake-category display/logic,
# even though the MOVE-based ground/climb physics itself is generic
# (see note above) -- the point of this file is the DEPARTURE TIMING,
# not per-type climb performance (that was validated separately via
# headless BADA simulation, see docx Sec.2 and the appendix table).

00:00:00.00>TRAILS ON
00:00:00.00>ASAS ON

